{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>As it vomited.</b> Past-tense verb from the root-pattern of שתו and שכרו and קיו, for the letters alef, he, vav, yod interchange. And there is ארץ in the masculine register — 'the land vomited them' (נעתם ארץ) and 'the land did not bear them.' Or היא is elliptically omitted, as if it were 'as it vomited,' like באה עם הצאן."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The phrase נעתם ארץ is textually difficult; translated hyper-literally. Possibly corrupt or elliptical. The root-pattern examples (שתו, שכרו, קיו) are Ibn Ezra's way of illustrating the consonantal template behind קאה."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:49.725133437Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}